<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	license:CC0-1.0

	Technics SX-WSA1R - acoustic modeling synthesizer module.

	The rack's panel is CP1/CP2, scanned by IC1 (M37471M2196S).  SEG0..SEG9 are
	its scan columns and SW0..SW7 its return rows; SEG6 (pin 40) and SEG10
	(pin 33) are unconnected stubs here, so segment_is_wired() in
	wsa1r_cpanel.cpp refuses them and nothing may bind to them.

	58 of the 80 matrix cells are populated: 47 on CP1 and 11 on CP2.  Not
	fitted, so neither drawn nor bound: SEG2/SW7 (SW24), SEG7/SW4..SW7,
	SEG8/SW2..SW7, SEG9/SW5..SW7.  Each button's comment names the source of
	its legend.

	18 lamps on the rack; 14 are named by the firmware's switch-to-LED table at
	Panel_SwitchLedTable_V2, whose word is (LED register << 8) | bit mask.  The driver's
	output index is register * 8 + bit, which is the led# used below.

	Drawn but not bound:
	  * the four REALTIME CREATOR ring lamps - the firmware pins the set to
	    {led16, led17, led24, led25} but not which is which.
	  * the floppy activity lamp - it belongs to the FDD, which exposes no
	    output.
	  * CONTRAST (VR2 on CP2) is an LCD bias pot wired to MAIN as VO, not a
	    panel-MCU input; POWER, PHONES and floppy eject have no ioport either.
	  * REALTIME CREATOR itself is board MB2's triple-gang VR2, reporting
	    JOYX/JOYY to the MAIN TMP95C061's A/D.  Only its ring lamps are on CP2.

	The prom_a addresses above refer to the OS v2.0 images; see the ROM record
	in wsa1.cpp.

	Firmware symbols used in the comments below.  Addresses are in the OS v2.0 images;
	a v1 OS shipped and is not dumped.

	    Panel_SwitchLedTable_V2 prom_a  0xF95088

	For the rack only.  The SX-WSA1 keyboard's panel is a different board with
	two extra scan columns and three extra pots.
-->
<mamelayout version="2">

	<element name="led_green" defstate="0">
		<disk state="0"><color red="0.00" green="0.19" blue="0.00"/></disk>
		<disk state="1"><color red="0.15" green="1.00" blue="0.15"/></disk>
	</element>

